    {
      "id": "ports-and-handles-as-authored-interface-geometry",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Projection Geometry",
      "position": {
        "x": 820,
        "y": 160
      },
      "width": 650,
      "height": 540,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ports-and-handles-as-authored-interface"
        },
        "markdown": "# Projection geometry\\n\\nLet the chosen node-body anchor have center `C = (cx, cy)`, width `w`, and height `h`. Let an authored Port or Handle primitive have center `Q = (qx, qy)`.\\n\\n1. Compute the relative vector `d = Q - C`.\\n2. Cast the ray from `C` through `Q`.\\n3. Intersect that ray with the anchor rectangle perimeter:\\n\\n`scale = min((w/2)/abs(dx), (h/2)/abs(dy))` using only defined nonzero terms.\\n\\n`P = C + scale * d`\\n\\n4. Convert `P` to a normalized perimeter coordinate.\\n5. At runtime, map that normalized coordinate onto the rendered node bounds or shape perimeter.\\n\\nThe authored graph therefore supplies one intuitive degree of freedom: **where the primitive is placed relative to the node body**. New contracts do not independently author `angle`, `side`, `offset`, and `radius`.\\n\\nSemantic role remains explicit. Geometry controls presentation, not whether the primitive receives or acts."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ports-and-handles-as-authored-interface-interface-map",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Authored Interface Map",
      "position": {
        "x": 820,
        "y": -500
      },
      "width": 650,
      "height": 500,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ports-and-handles-as-authored-interface"
        },
        "markdown": "# Authored node interface\\n\\n```text\\n                    [Handle: History]\\n                           | creates\\n[Port: Source]   [Root or Title Surface]   [Handle: Applications]\\n  accepts any                                | creates\\n                           |                 v\\n                    [Handle: Definitions]  [Wikipedia Section Class]\\n```\\n\\n- **Port primitives** describe what the node listens for.\\n- **Handle primitives** describe available graph actions.\\n- **Handle -> Port** is the canonical connection direction.\\n- **Handle -> class/surface/capability** relationships describe behavior.\\n- Primitive placement around the surface becomes instance perimeter placement.\\n\\nThe title/root surface is not merely decoration: it may become the spatial anchor and the navigation affordance into the graph that defines the node."
      }
    },
